    "manufacturer_status": "active",
    "name": "AdMore Light Bar Pro",
    "notes": "Bluetooth-enabled motorcycle brake light bar with accelerometer-based smart braking. Uses Nordic UART Service (NUS) with protobuf-encoded messages. Full Flutter app reverse engineering of AdMore Connect v2.1.0 (code 44). App framework: Flutter/Dart with flutter_blue_plus, GetX, package:protobuf. 14 protobuf message types, 7 enums (complete values), KMsg routing with 36 route IDs. Protobuf field numbers extracted via blutter (Dart SDK 3.3.3). All 14 message names and all 7 enum names are present as string constants in libapp.so (app-confirmed). DFU (app-derived, not hardware-verified): the device advertises as \"AdMore Light Bar DFU\" in update mode and the app drives a Nordic legacy DFU through the flutter nordic_dfu plugin. The app ships a debug DFU package (assets/debug/debug_dfu.zip) in the legacy bin+dat manifest format containing a 49,640-byte nRF52 application image — the first firmware artifact seen for this device, pinning the SoC family to Nordic nRF52.\n",
